\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Uniform acceleration, with $x={\bm  {\mathrm  {u}}}\cdot {\bm  {\mathrm  {r}}}$ and $x'={\bm  {\mathrm  {u}}}\cdot {\bm  {\mathrm  {r}}}'$. Top: the same grid and light rays in inertial and accelerated coordinates. The three solid worldlines have $\dot  v_0x'=-1/2,0,1$; thin connecting lines are simultaneous at fixed $t'$. Dotted light rays leave $O$; the additional dotted null line on the left is the future horizon. Hatching excludes $1+\dot  v_0x'\le 0$. Short V shapes show local coordinate cones: their width varies with position, while locally measured light speed is $1$. Bottom left: fixed grid clocks accumulate different proper times. Bottom right: between the same events $O$ and $E:(\dot  v_0x,\dot  v_0t)=(1/4,3/4)$, the accelerated clock records $\ln (2)/\dot  v_0$, less than the inertial clock's $1/(\sqrt  2\dot  v_0)$. Thus finite event separation and elapsed time along a curved path differ.}}{53}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:observer-rindler}{{6}{53}{Uniform acceleration, with $x=\bu \dotprod \br $ and $x'=\bu \dotprod \br '$. Top: the same grid and light rays in inertial and accelerated coordinates. The three solid worldlines have $\dot v_0x'=-1/2,0,1$; thin connecting lines are simultaneous at fixed $t'$. Dotted light rays leave $O$; the additional dotted null line on the left is the future horizon. Hatching excludes $1+\dot v_0x'\le 0$. Short V shapes show local coordinate cones: their width varies with position, while locally measured light speed is $1$. Bottom left: fixed grid clocks accumulate different proper times. Bottom right: between the same events $O$ and $E:(\dot v_0x,\dot v_0t)=(1/4,3/4)$, the accelerated clock records $\ln (2)/\dot v_0$, less than the inertial clock's $1/(\sqrt 2\dot v_0)$. Thus finite event separation and elapsed time along a curved path differ}{figure.6}{}}
